  "topic_non_degeneracy_note": "The 2% floor is applied to the TRAIN split, which is where the clustering is fitted and where 'six usable groups' is a property of the partition. val/test hold only 61/63 documents and wikitext-103 shares them byte-for-byte with wikitext-2, so one small cluster contributing a single val document is ~1.1% of val blocks and a 2% floor there could never pass for this corpus family. Their shares are stored above because that thinness is a real limitation of the article-level agreement in T-L6.6.",
